.TH "nvme_init_sanitize_nvm" 9 "nvme_init_sanitize_nvm" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
nvme_init_sanitize_nvm \- Initialize passthru command to start a sanitize operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" nvme_init_sanitize_nvm
.BI "(struct libnvme_passthru_cmd *cmd "  ","
.BI "enum nvme_sanitize_sanact sanact "  ","
.BI "bool ause "  ","
.BI "__u8 owpass "  ","
.BI "bool oipbp "  ","
.BI "bool ndas "  ","
.BI "bool emvs "  ","
.BI "bool preq "  ","
.BI "__u32 ovrpat "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "cmd" 12
Passthru command to use
.IP "sanact" 12
Sanitize action, see \fIenum nvme_sanitize_sanact\fP
.IP "ause" 12
Set to allow unrestricted sanitize exit
.IP "owpass" 12
Overwrite pass count
.IP "oipbp" 12
Set to overwrite invert pattern between passes
.IP "ndas" 12
Set to not deallocate blocks after sanitizing
.IP "emvs" 12
Set to enter media verification state
.IP "preq" 12
Set to require the sanitize operation to purge user data, as
defined by IEEE Std 2883, or fail
.IP "ovrpat" 12
Overwrite pattern
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Initializes the passthru command buffer for the Sanitize NVM command.
